## Interface: 30300
## Title: Item Browser
## Notes: Browse every item on the realm with auction-house filters, real item tooltips, and one button to hand an item to your target.
## Author: wowserver
## Version: 2.0
## SavedVariables: ItemBrowserSaved
## DefaultState: enabled

# Load order matters.
#   Data.lua declares ItemBrowserData and the Chunk() the generated shards call, so it must
#   come before Data\Data.xml.
#   Data\Data.xml is GENERATED (tools/itemdb.py) and lists the shard files. Pointing the .toc
#   at the XML rather than at the shards means changing --shard-rows never edits this file.
#   UI.xml pulls in UI.lua, Tree.lua and Launcher.lua itself, in that order, before it
#   declares any widget -- so every OnLoad handler the templates name already exists.
#
# Bindings.xml is deliberately NOT listed: the client loads an addon's Bindings.xml by itself,
# and naming it here would load it twice.
Data.lua
Data\Data.xml
Search.lua
Transport.lua
UI.xml
